# Upload filter for `gcloud builds submit` (root-context builds).
#
# CD builds every service with the REPO ROOT as the Docker context, because the services
# that consume @bharattruck/shared via a `file:../packages/shared` dependency (auth,
# booking, tracking) cannot resolve it from a single-service context. That means the whole repo is uploaded
# to Cloud Build on every deploy, so this file is what keeps that upload small.
#
# NOTE: unlike .dockerignore, the presence of this file makes gcloud STOP honouring
# .gitignore. Everything that should not ship must therefore be listed here explicitly.

.git
.gitignore

# Dependencies — always reinstalled inside the image from the lockfile. Uploading these
# would add hundreds of MB and, worse, could leak a host-built (darwin) binary into a
# linux image.
**/node_modules

# Build output. Services recompile in the builder stage.
# EXCEPTION: packages/shared/dist is COMMITTED and is the actual artifact consumers
# install (its package.json has `files: ["dist"]`), so it must NOT be excluded.
**/.next
bt-*/dist

# Local env + tooling noise
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
.claude
.review-worktrees
**/.DS_Store
**/*.log
**/.turbo
**/coverage

# Docs and scripts are not build inputs
docs
scripts
